IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `taa-types`
IMPORT `taa-dates`
IMPORT `taa-returns`
IMPORT `taa-penalties`

-- Tax Administration Act 1994 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For a taxpayer and a tax year: must they file, by when (and to when may
--    time be extended), what late filing penalty applies, what late payment
--    penalty has accrued by a date, what shortfall penalty applies, and until
--    when may the Commissioner increase the assessment?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Administration position` HAS
    `must file a return`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `return due on`                                     IS A DATE
    `latest extended due date through a tax agent`      IS A DATE
    `late filing penalty`                               IS A NUMBER
    `late payment penalty`                              IS A NUMBER
    `shortfall penalty`                                 IS A NUMBER
    -- NOTHING: no return yet, or no time bar (s 108(2)).
    `last day to increase the assessment`               IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 33, 37, 108, 139A, 139B, 141A-141K, 141JAA
@export default A taxpayer's position for a tax year under the Tax Administration Act 1994 (NZ): whether they must file a return (s 33), its due date and the latest date to which a tax agent's extension may run (s 37), the late filing penalty (s 139A), the late payment penalty accrued by a date on any unpaid tax (s 139B), the shortfall penalty on any tax shortfall (ss 141A-141K, 141JAA), and the last day the Commissioner may increase the assessment (s 108). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A Filer  @desc The tax year, exempt-only income, any approved income year end, the filing date and net income
      notified IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the Commissioner has notified that a late filing penalty is payable
      unpaid IS A MAYBE `Late payment facts`  @desc Any unpaid tax, with its default date, payment and the s 139B(1) facts
      shortfall IS A MAYBE `Shortfall facts`  @desc Any tax shortfall, with culpability, disclosures and history
      fraud IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the return was fraudulent or wilfully misleading, or omitted income of a particular nature or source
      asAt IS A DATE  @desc The day at which the position is measured
GIVETH AN `Administration position`
`the administration position for` f `, penalty notified` notified `, unpaid tax` unpaid `, shortfall` shortfall `, fraud or omission` fraud `, as at` asAt MEANS
    `Administration position` WITH
        `must file a return`                            IS mustFile
        `return due on`                                 IS due
        `latest extended due date through a tax agent`  IS `the latest extended due date for the return of` f
        `late filing penalty`                           IS IF mustFile THEN `the late filing penalty for` `an annual tax return` `, net income` (f's `net income for the year`) `, late` late `, notified` notified ELSE 0
        `late payment penalty`                          IS
            CONSIDER unpaid
            WHEN JUST p THEN `the late payment penalty on` p `, as at` asAt
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        `shortfall penalty`                             IS
            CONSIDER shortfall
            WHEN JUST s THEN `the shortfall penalty for` s
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        `last day to increase the assessment`           IS
            CONSIDER f's `return filed on`
            WHEN JUST filed THEN `the last day to increase the assessment, return provided` filed `, fraud or omission` fraud
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        mustFile MEANS `must file a return of income` f
        due MEANS `the due date for the return of` f
        late MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `return filed on`
            WHEN JUST filed THEN filed GREATER THAN due
            WHEN NOTHING THEN asAt GREATER THAN due
